[DONE] saving the floor plan is quite slow. could be `cargo run` dev mode. investigate to make sure there aren't other issues
  Root cause was NOT dev mode (that adds only constant overhead). The real issue: each save handler deleted then re-inserted rows one statement at a time in a loop (plan_tiles, plan_walls, plan_lights, plan_rooms, plan_room_tiles), and each statement ran as its own autocommit transaction under SQLite's default synchronous=FULL — i.e. one fsync per row. A plan with hundreds–thousands of painted tiles = hundreds–thousands of fsyncs → multi-second saves even in release.

  Fixes:
  - Wrapped set_layout / set_lights / set_rooms each in a single transaction (state.db.begin → … → commit), so the whole replace commits with one fsync instead of one per row. (set_rooms' inner room SELECT/UPDATE/INSERT now run on the txn too, which is also more consistent.)
  - Pool pragmas (src/db/mod.rs): journal_mode=WAL, synchronous=NORMAL, busy_timeout=5s — commits append to the WAL and fsync only at checkpoint, plus better write concurrency.

  Other paths checked: get_plan reads are already bulk fetch_all (no N+1); load_rooms does one tiles query per region (bounded by region count, negligible); the frontend save is 5 sequential calls (3 writes + reload + rooms) but each is now fast. All 97 lib + 83 integration tests green.
